WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.541
SPEAKER: In this
Cloud Minute, you'll

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:04.840
learn how to quickly deploy a
Java Web Application to Google

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.340
App Engine Standard with Maven.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.070
First, add the
App Engine plug-in

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:15.090
to [? pump.xml. ?] Then, create
an app engine web.xml file

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.760
and specify Java 8 as
the App Engine run type.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.140
App Engine [? extender ?]
now supports servlet 3.1,

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.470
so you can annotate
your servlets.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.800
You can also use all of the
Java 8 API's end features,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.990
such as string and lambdas.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.750
Finally, deploy the
application using Maven.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.330
Once deployed, you can
access the application

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.200
with the project's URL on
[? appspa.com. ?] You can also

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.130
deploy this application
directly from Gradle, IntelliJ,

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.210
or Eclipse using
respective plug-ins.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.460
Learn more on the
Google Cloud Platform

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.010
for Java developer's website.

